# IP URL suspicious — regexp map for arbitrary IPv4/IPv6 literal hostnames
# Matches URLs using raw IP addresses instead of domain names
# Rspamd canonicalizes URL hostnames: IPv4 as dotted quad, IPv6 without brackets
# Format: regexp patterns (one per line)

# IPv4: digits.digits.digits.digits
^(?:[0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}$

# IPv6: hex colons (with optional ::), no brackets (Rspamd canonicalizes without [])
^[0-9a-fA-F:]*::?[0-9a-fA-F:]*$

# IPv6 with brackets (in case some inputs retain them)
^\[[0-9a-fA-F:]+\]$
